CONTEXT City INCLUDES Registry FROM "../contexts/registry_with_towns.adl",
                      Shops FROM "../contexts/shops.adl"
CONTEXT City IN ENGLISH
PURPOSE CONTEXT City
{+ A diamond: the register of persons and the register of shops both include the context Towns.
Towns is one context with one database, so the town of a shop and the town in which a person lives
are atoms of one concept, and a rule can compose the two relations. +}

RELATION customer[Shops.Shop*Registry.Person]
POPULATION customer[Shops.Shop*Registry.Person] CONTAINS [ ("s1", "p1") ]

RULE local : customer |- Shops.located;Registry.residence~
MEANING "A customer lives in the town of the shop."
ROLE Clerk MAINTAINS local

ENDCONTEXT
